" vimrc - the system vimrc of vim on AMIX and Atari System V
" (atari-sysv-sp1 amix/vim), installed as /usr/local/share/vim/vimrc.
"
" Neither system has a UTF-8 locale, so vim would take 'encoding' latin1
" from the locale. Text is UTF-8 inside vim instead (mail is, and most of
" what comes from the network), while the terminal stays what the locale
" says: Latin-1, unless LANG names UTF-8. vim converts between the two
" itself; what Latin-1 can't show comes out as "?".
if &encoding !=# 'utf-8'
  let &termencoding = &encoding
  set encoding=utf-8
endif

" The backtracking regexp engine, not the NFA one. When a file is opened,
" vim compiles the file name patterns of filetype.vim (over a thousand).
" As NFA programs they take some 18 MB here, more than AMIX lets a process
" have (16 MB) and than the machines have; as backtracking ones, about 1 MB.
set regexpengine=1

" More time to colour a screen before vim gives up on a buffer's syntax
" (2 s by default): on the TT's 68030 a screen of quoted mail takes 2-2.5 s,
" even with vimfiles/after/syntax/mail.vim.
set redrawtime=6000
